title: 'network-gossip: Don''t refresh known messages during garbage collection'
doc:
- audience:
  - Node Dev
  - Node Operator
  description: |-
    `ConsensusGossip::collect_garbage` trims every peer's `known_messages` against the global `known_messages` LRU.

    It used `LruMap::get` for the lookup, which marks the entry as recently used.
    Since the trim runs on every periodic maintenance (1.1s) and covers every hash any peer knows, the LRU stops tracking when messages were registered.

    Eviction then depends on which hashes peers happen to know, not on age.

    This PR switches the lookup to `peek`, which leaves the order untouched

    Found while looking into #11540.

    ### Testing

      - `collect_garbage_does_not_refresh_known_messages`: fills the cache, runs garbage collection
        with the oldest message known by a peer, then checks that this message is the one evicted
        next. Fails without the fix.
      - `message_broadcast_by_validator_is_stored_once`: covers the validator re-broadcast path.
      - `cargo test -p sc-network-gossip`
crates:
- name: sc-network-gossip
  bump: patch
